{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`scripts/check_config_reads.py` proves every `_config_schema.py` field is consumed, but nothing proves the OPPOSITE: that ONLY approved composition roots / provider boundaries read ambient config and credentials — so a new below-seam `load_config`/`os.getenv` read, or a new credential name with no owner, can silently appear. `gen_env_registry.py` already implements AST env-read detection + one-level helper-shim resolution (`KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS`), and documents (bug b00f) that a helper ABSENT from that table is INVISIBLE. This gate REUSES that machinery rather than duplicating and drifting from it.\n\n## Outcome\nA deterministic AST gate `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` (mirroring `check_config_reads.py`'s `check(root)->list[str]` / `main(argv)->int` contract and `# read-via: <pointer>` escape-marker style) that, for every `src/rebar` module NOT in the approved-seam set, flags each prohibited category below. An explicit registry enumerates approved composition roots + provider-credential boundaries and DERIVES its owner sets from existing registries (no duplicate). Test-only controls/protocol constants are allowed only via exact `path + symbol + rationale` entries (never path globs). An initial legacy-exception set enumerates current below-seam reads so the gate is introducible without touching product code; C3 (075b) drains it to empty.\n\n### Prohibited categories — concrete AST detection rules\nEach fires only when the enclosing module path is NOT an approved seam for that category. \"Resolved callee\" = after import/local-alias resolution (Plan step 2).\n1. **Ambient env read** — reuse `gen_env_registry`'s matchers: `_is_os_environ` subscripted or `.get(...)`, and `os.getenv(...)` `Call` with string-literal key. Resolved env-name captured for cats 5–6.\n2. **Helper-shim env read** — `Call` whose resolved callee is a key of `gen_env_registry.KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS`; env-name resolved one level via that table's row (IMPORTED — single source). A shim-shaped callee (leading `_` + `env`/`pref`/`getenv`) ABSENT from the table, or any env read whose name arg is NOT a literal (dynamic), is reported `unresolved-env-read` — the gate FAILS CLOSED where the doc-generator silently skips (closes b00f for gate use).\n3. **`load_config` call** — `Call` whose resolved callee is `load_config` (direct, `from ...config import load_config`, or local `lc = load_config; lc(...)`) in a module not an approved composition root.\n4. **Literal-`getattr` env equivalent** — `getattr(<recv>, <literal>, ...)` where `<recv>` resolves to `os.environ`; treated as cat 1 with the constant as env-name.\n5. **Provider-credential read** — a cat-1/2/4 read whose resolved env-name is in the credential-name set from `_child_env.owned_secret_names()`/`_ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES`, outside the approved provider-credential boundary set.\n6. **Configurable adapter default / backend reload** — (a) a module-level assignment or function default-arg whose RHS is any prohibited access of cats 1–5; (b) a `Call` whose resolved callee is a `_backend_registry` selector/accessor (`select_backend`, `register`, or direct `_REGISTRY` read) in a module not an approved provider boundary.\n\n### Approved seams (two DISTINCT sets) + owner-registry derivation\nOwner sets are DERIVED at run time from existing registries, not hand-copied:\n- **Composition roots** (own cats 1–4 config reads): `*/config.py`, `_config_sources.py`, `_child_env.py`, and LLM model adapters `anthropic_model.py`/`bedrock_model.py` (own their LLM env `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`/bedrock vars — NOT JIRA credentials).\n- **Provider-credential boundaries** (own cat-5 reads): `rebar_reconciler/runtime.py`, `.../adapters/jira_datacenter/settings.py`, `.../adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py` — the real readers of `JIRA_API_TOKEN`/`JIRA_PAT` (per docs/env-vars.md), enumerated as approved owners (how they SOURCE the value is C3's concern; not a legacy exception).\n- **Credential names** ← `_child_env.owned_secret_names()` (union of `_ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES`), mapped to owning adapter + boundary module.\n- **Adapters/backends** ← an AST scan for `@register(<literal>)` decorators under `.../adapters/` (static, offline). NOT `_backend_registry._REGISTRY`, which is EMPTY at plain import time (adapters self-register only via the lazy `import rebar_reconciler.adapters` inside `select_backend`).\n- **Declared-env baseline** ← union of `gen_env_registry.scan(src/rebar)` names and `_deprecations.REGISTRY(kind==\"env\")`. \"Newly declared\" = a spelling/credential name the scan surfaces that maps to NO owner → gate fails naming it.\n\n## Plan\n1. **Reuse, don't re-implement.** Import `scan`/`KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS`/`_is_os_environ`/`_str_literal` from `gen_env_registry.py` (or extract into a shared `scripts/_env_scan.py` both import — one authoritative \"what counts as an env read\"). Only cats 3/4/6 get new logic.\n2. **Alias/receiver resolution** per module: track `import ... as`, `from ... import name`, and local `x = <callee>` bindings so direct / import-aliased / local-aliased forms resolve to one canonical callee.\n3. **Approved-seam + owner registry**: enumerate the two seam sets and derive owner sets as specified above; reject path-glob exceptions STRUCTURALLY (any exception `path` with a glob metachar or naming a directory).\n4. **Diagnostic** reports `path`, `symbol`, `access kind`, `owning seam` (or UNOWNED).\n5. **Legacy-exception set**: exact `path+symbol+rationale` entries for current below-seam reads; C3 drains to empty.\n6. **Fixtures + self-tests** (see Testing).\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- Synthetic fixtures for direct/import-aliased/local-aliased forms and EACH category 1–6 (incl. `getattr(os.environ,...)`, an unresolved dynamic read, a shim-shaped call absent from the table, a credential read outside its boundary, a below-seam `select_backend`) each fail with the expected `path/symbol/access-kind/owning-seam` diagnostic.\n- Self-tests: a new bypass, a new unowned name (added to `_ADAPTER_SECRET_NAMES` or a new env spelling), a path-glob exception, or a missing rationale each fail with the expected diagnostic. The unowned-name case doubles as the drift self-test (proves derivation is live, not a snapshot).\n- Clean approved fixtures pass with no findings.\n- Runs OFFLINE, no network/CI: `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` exits 0 on the current tree, 1 on a synthetic violation.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nAdditive: not wired into `make lint`/CI (C2, 735b); product code unchanged (C3, 075b). Reusing/extracting `gen_env_registry.py`'s scanner leaves that generator's `--check` output unchanged. Rollback deletes the new script/registry/fixtures (and `_env_scan.py` if created, restoring the inline copy).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each of the 6 categories has a concrete AST rule (per Outcome) and a synthetic fixture — direct, import-aliased, local-aliased included — failing with `path`, `symbol`, `access kind`, expected owning seam; clean approved fixtures pass.\n- [ ] Env-read detection + shim resolution REUSE `gen_env_registry`'s `scan`/`KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS` (imported or shared-extracted), not a parallel parser; a shim-shaped callee absent from the table and a dynamic env read fail CLOSED as `unresolved-env-read`.\n- [ ] The owner registry DERIVES credential names from `_child_env`, backend keys from a static `@register(<literal>)` decorator scan (NOT the import-time-empty `_REGISTRY`), env baseline from `gen_env_registry.scan` + `_deprecations.REGISTRY(kind==\"env\")`; the provider-credential boundary set (reconciler runtime + jira settings/acli) is enumerated distinctly from composition roots; a newly declared spelling/credential name lacking an owner fails (drift self-test); path-glob exceptions rejected structurally.\n- [ ] Exposes `check(root)->list[str]` and `main(argv)->int`, is unit-tested, runs offline with no CI/network dependency, exits 0 on the current tree (initial exact-entry legacy-exception set covers current reads; C3 drains it)."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787083056970968001,"uuid":"87c82c2a-5bdc-4b8a-8bff-fc3c1806ab8e"}